    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0448" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4434</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ewing</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-07T12:00:00-05:48">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 5 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In an interview with the President of the Republic, Saturday, I received
                    assurance of Honduran cooperation in every way possible without violation of
                    treaty of Washington which Honduras considers as obligating her to be the last
                    of Central-American states to become belligerent. The President stated that
                    Honduras has not made any alliance and will not unless with the United
                    States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ewing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
